.TH BANDWIDTH-USAGE-RUN-REPORT 8 "2026-10-01" "bandwidth-usage-systemd 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bandwidth-usage-run-report \- run the packaged bandwidth usage reporter for the receiver service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bandwidth-usage-run-report
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bandwidth-usage-run-report
is the receiver-side helper used by
.BR bandwidth-usage-report.service .
It reads
.IR /etc/sysconfig/bandwidth-usage ,
builds the correct reporter command line, and executes
.BR bandwidth-usage-report (1).
.PP
The helper is installed under
.IR /usr/libexec/bandwidth-usage .
Operators normally run it through systemd:
.PP
.nf
systemctl start bandwidth-usage-report.service
.fi
.PP
Do not configure the service to call
.I /opt/bandwidth-usage-reporter/bw_rpts_report.py
directly. The
.I /opt
tree belongs to the reporter package's isolated runtime. Direct invocation with
the system Python interpreter bypasses that runtime and can fail unless
NumPy/SciPy are installed separately. The intended service interface is this
helper, which invokes the supported
.I /usr/bin/bandwidth-usage-report
wrapper.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The helper reads these optional shell variables from
.IR /etc/sysconfig/bandwidth-usage :
.TP
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_SPOOL_DIR
Input directory containing monthly and daily vnStat exports. Default:
.IR /var/spool/bandwidth-usage .
.TP
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_OUTPUT_DIR
Directory for generated JSON and PostScript output. Default:
.IR /var/spool/bandwidth-usage/.cache .
.TP
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_REPORT
Reporter executable. Default:
.IR /usr/bin/bandwidth-usage-report .
.TP
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_PRINT
Whether to print the report. Accepted true values are
.IR 1 ,
.IR yes ,
.IR true ,
and
.IR on .
Accepted false values are
.IR 0 ,
.IR no ,
.IR false ,
and
.IR off .
The default is
.IR 1 .
.TP
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_LPR_OPTIONS
Whitespace-separated options passed to
.BR lpr (1)
when printing is enabled. Default:
.IR "-o fit-to-page=true" .
.TP
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_REPORT_DATE
Explicit report date in
.I YYYY-MM-DD
or
.I YYMMDD
format. When empty, the reporter infers the date from the newest daily vnStat
row.
.SH INPUTS
Input files are read from
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_SPOOL_DIR .
The underlying reporter expects one monthly and one daily vnStat JSON or CSV
export. See
.BR bandwidth-usage-report (1)
for accepted file names.
.SH OUTPUTS
Generated report files are written to
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_OUTPUT_DIR .
The default files are:
.TP
.I bandwidth_usage.YYMMDD.json
Normalized and scored report data.
.TP
.I bandwidth_usage.YYMMDD.ps
Rendered PostScript report.
.PP
When printing is enabled, the PostScript file is submitted to
.BR lpr (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Report generation succeeded.
.TP
.B 2
.B BANDWIDTH_USAGE_PRINT
had an invalid value.
.TP
.B non-zero
Directory creation, reporter execution, input parsing, scoring, rendering, or
printing failed. The service journal records standard output and standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sysconfig/bandwidth-usage
Receiver configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/bandwidth-usage-report.service
Oneshot service that invokes this helper as
.IR bandwidth-usage:bandwidth-usage .
.TP
.I /var/spool/bandwidth-usage
Default input spool.
.TP
.I /var/spool/bandwidth-usage/.cache
Default output directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bandwidth-usage-report (1),
.BR systemd.path (5),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR lpr (1)
